        text: Existing functionality from R1.x through R3.x is not broken\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/comm -- srd029 R1.1-R1.4\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd029-comm.yaml (full SRD -- focus on requirement group R1)\n      - CLAUDE.md (project patterns, build instructions, SIGPIPE, differential testing)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests function signature)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/comm/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: Initial comm implementation covering srd029 R1.1-R1.4\n      - path: cmd/comm/comm_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests for R1.1-R1.4\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement srd029-comm requirement R1.1 as specified in the SRD\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement srd029-comm requirement R1.2 as specified in the SRD\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement srd029-comm requirement R1.3 as specified in the SRD\n      - id: R4\n        text: Implement srd029-comm requirement R1.4 as specified in the SRD\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Create cmd/comm/main.go with a main function that calls sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start, per project SIGPIPE convention.\n      - id: D2\n        text: Use the differential testing pattern with pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests against the gcomm reference binary (exec.LookPath(\"gcomm\")). Skip tests if not found.\n      - id: D3\n        text: Build the binary in tests using testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\"). Build output goes to bin/ directory.\n      - id: D4\n        text: Structure the implementation to accept later extension for R2.x through R4.x requirements without rewriting core logic.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: cmd/comm/main.go exists and implements R1.1-R1.4 from srd029-comm\n      - id: AC2\n        text: cmd/comm/comm_test.go exists 